  "readme": "# Closed UI31 ordinary-directory evidence\n\nOriginal session7407 completed with original exit0/chunk118237 at data epoch2b79f24746e208bab0824335595be3b2109771c4 and source6630ac70f17332efa031d021af00532d42307568. Later cleanup, character-publication and archive-parent commits are not substituted for that runtime epoch. Root independently verified33488 input paths and actual process/port/profile closure before releasing the write hold.\n\nAll31 requested sections completed:144 API/DOM cards,129 loaded native scenes and15 expected missing-script cards,16 portals,119 API/DOM line/hit paths,119 edges/238 measured endpoints with zero endpoint distance.116/119 edges had positive finite sampled hits. Three remain observed-unproven. No all-edge positive-hit or real edge-click activation claim is made. Exact original samples and geometry appear in the offline fact packet.\n\nOne original external fetch error and one original external console error retain positive context/realm provenance. Causes remain unknown. allNetworkClean and allConsoleClean remain false; strict same-origin fetch/console errors and JavaScript exceptions were zero. Complete raw diagnostics and indexes are losslessly retained. Original failed36551 and prior failed trials remain failed.\n\nThe complete runtime guard inventory has exactly one lossless gzip entry. Kitv2, source-only peers, collectorv4/peer, original journals/logs, release and root closure retain their source hashes. This adds evidence only; it accepts no new script fields, assets, frontend/deployment changes, source acting, pixels, timing, media, continuous gameplay or complete restoration.\n\nThe complete local general-process snapshots are intentionally not copied to this external audit because they include unrelated user application command lines. Their exact hashes remain in the root approval; complete owned-process, PID/PGID, profile, port and independent closure evidence is included. Original network and console diagnostic arrays are retained without dropping records.\n\nThe first unpublished archive encountered a source README trailing-blank-line diff-check failure. The complete original README is now stored as gzip, with identical decoded bytes. Original source and prior failed evidence remain unchanged; no diff-check rule was disabled and no business or browser invocation was replayed.\n",
